            <ArticleTitle>[A patient with a diaphragmatic mass].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>381-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cystic teratoma of the diaphragm is a rare, generally asymptomatic, disease. We report a case which was disclosed by the development of fever and pain in the left hypochondria. Imaging ruled out surgical emergency and led to the diagnosis, describing the relations of the tumor.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
